cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using these metadata."
title: >-
  sundogcert: A machine-checked 3SAT <= 3DM <= X3C <= syndrome-decoding
  hardness chain in Lean 4
abstract: >-
  An axiom-clean Lean 4 / mathlib formalization of the reduction-correctness
  spine of the classical Karp chain 3SAT <= 3DM <= X3C <= bounded-weight GF(2)
  syndrome decoding, with each link proved as a both-directions equivalence,
  the syndrome-certificate core it lands on, and a build-enforced axiom gate
  pinning every headline theorem to Lean's three foundational axioms. The
  repository additionally carries related Lean method-demonstration modules
  (real-analysis shadow decay, halo minimum-deviation geometry, Aharonov-Bohm
  gauge invariance). Reproducible by `lake build` (Lean v4.30.0, mathlib v4.30.0).
type: software
authors:
